+## Uploading files
+
+`client.Files.Upload` takes a file name and a reader and builds the
+`multipart/form-data` body for you. Because it buffers the upload into a
+replayable body, the request participates in the retry policy above — a 429 or
+5xx during a bulk import is retried instead of failing immediately:
+
+```go
+f, err := os.Open("contract.pdf")
+if err != nil {
+	// handle error
+}
+defer f.Close()
+
+file, err := client.Files.Upload(context.Background(), "contract.pdf", f)
+```
+
+For full control over the payload, `client.Files.Add` still accepts a pre-built
+body and `Content-Type` — note that it can only be retried when the body is a
+type `net/http` can rewind (such as a `*bytes.Reader`).
+
